 ## Background
-Not given in the sources.
+Signed Distance Functions have been a cornerstone of geometric modeling and rendering for decades. The family article [S1] cites "DIST: Rendering Deep Implicit Signed Distance Function With Differentiable Sphere Tracing" (2020) as a key reference for differentiable rendering of SDFs. The use of SDFs for volume rendering, particularly converting SDFs to density, is discussed in [S4] and . The application of SDFs in robotics and dynamic scenes is covered in [S1] and [S5]. The use of auto-encoders for TSDF compression is detailed in [S4]. The joint learning of implicit surfaces and meshing is presented in [S2]. The handling of sign-ambiguous geometry via Metric-Phase Fields is introduced in [S3, unofficial].
 
